

## Complete Git Workflow (CMD)

```bash
:: STEP 1 - Go to Desktop
cd Desktop

:: STEP 2 - Create Folder Structure
mkdir "06-Week 6"
cd "06-Week 6"
mkdir "Git-HOL -1"
cd "Git-HOL -1"

:: STEP 3 - Initialize Git Repository
git init

:: STEP 4 - Check Initial Status
git status

:: STEP 5 - Create Files
type nul > welcome.txt
type nul > week6.txt

:: STEP 6 - Open File and Add Content
notepad welcome.txt

:: STEP 7 - Check Status (Untracked Files)
git status

:: STEP 8 - Add Files to Staging Area
git add .

:: STEP 9 - Verify Staging
git status

:: STEP 10 - Commit Files
git commit -m "Week 6 Git HOL completed"

:: STEP 11 - View Commit History
git log

:: STEP 12 - Remove Old Remote (if exists)
git remote remove origin

:: STEP 13 - Add Remote Repository
git remote add origin https://github.com/riyaashukla30/Digital-Nurture-Exercises.git

:: STEP 14 - Verify Remote
git remote -v

:: STEP 15 - Pull Existing Data from GitHub
git pull origin main --rebase

:: STEP 16 - Rename Branch to Main
git branch -M main

:: STEP 17 - Push Code to GitHub
git push -u origin main
```

